      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In each year's annual Appropriations Act, Congress has prohibited the Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco, and Firearms from investigating or acting upon applications for discretionary relief from firearms disabilities under 18 U.S.C. 925(c.)"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Rehnquist",
      "case_id": "2002-01-704",
      "confidence": 0.97,
      "document_hash": "7331b4fdf4753cd41dffe6b73240c1d1f6b77a6db97e9d813085b260a968f50c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7331b4fdf475-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Mr. Kneedler --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Rehnquist",
      "case_id": "2002-01-704",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "7331b4fdf4753cd41dffe6b73240c1d1f6b77a6db97e9d813085b260a968f50c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7331b4fdf475-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE REHNQUIST: We'll hear argument now in Number 01-704, United States v. Bean. Mr. Kneedler."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Tommy Bean (Respondent)",
      "case_id": "2002-01-704",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "7331b4fdf4753cd41dffe6b73240c1d1f6b77a6db97e9d813085b260a968f50c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7331b4fdf475-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The obvious flaw in the Government's position this morning, as several of the later questions identified, is that Congress has never, expressly or impliedly repealed those rights vis a vis the Secretary."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2002-01-704",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7331b4fdf4753cd41dffe6b73240c1d1f6b77a6db97e9d813085b260a968f50c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7331b4fdf475-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Well, now, did your client seek to proceed before the Secretary?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2002-01-704",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7331b4fdf4753cd41dffe6b73240c1d1f6b77a6db97e9d813085b260a968f50c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7331b4fdf475-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Now, Justice Ginsburg, one of the premises of your question was that there's a delegation here. The delegation here is not exclusive. The delegation here provides that -- and this was in 19 -- when the BATF was created, the Secretary provided that the Director shall act under the general supervision of the Secretary and under -- excuse me, and under the supervision of the Assistant Secretary."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2002-01-704",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7331b4fdf4753cd41dffe6b73240c1d1f6b77a6db97e9d813085b260a968f50c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7331b4fdf475-0001-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the district judge orders the United States and the Secretary made the party defendant."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2002-01-704",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7331b4fdf4753cd41dffe6b73240c1d1f6b77a6db97e9d813085b260a968f50c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7331b4fdf475-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Government did press its argument that there wasn't jurisdiction, but it absolutely did participate on the factual side of the case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2002-01-704",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7331b4fdf4753cd41dffe6b73240c1d1f6b77a6db97e9d813085b260a968f50c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7331b4fdf475-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I don't know that that's an argument. I mean, I concede that. I'm still left back at Justice Scalia's question, because I thought in response to his question you -- I had the impression you were suggesting that the Secretary had somewhere written a piece of paper that in effect denied the application, and I looked through this appendix -- I've been doing that and listening at the same time --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2002-01-704",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7331b4fdf4753cd41dffe6b73240c1d1f6b77a6db97e9d813085b260a968f50c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7331b4fdf475-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: I don't know that that was the"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Goldstein",
      "case_id": "2002-01-704",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7331b4fdf4753cd41dffe6b73240c1d1f6b77a6db97e9d813085b260a968f50c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7331b4fdf475-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The very best we think that the Government can get out of this argument is a judgment of this Court that says we were entitled to a remand to the Secretary."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2002-01-704",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7331b4fdf4753cd41dffe6b73240c1d1f6b77a6db97e9d813085b260a968f50c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7331b4fdf475-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Because otherwise Congress can't work."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Kneedler",
      "case_id": "2002-01-704",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7331b4fdf4753cd41dffe6b73240c1d1f6b77a6db97e9d813085b260a968f50c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7331b4fdf475-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We think that principle should apply a fortiori, or at least it's a reasonable interpretation for the Secretary to make, that when Congress has prohibited the expenditure of any funds by the agency to whom the Secretary has delegated that authority, that Congress did not expect money to be drawn from some other pot."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Rehnquist",
      "case_id": "2002-01-704",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7331b4fdf4753cd41dffe6b73240c1d1f6b77a6db97e9d813085b260a968f50c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7331b4fdf475-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE REHNQUIST: Thank you, Mr. Kneedler. The case is submitted."
    }
  ],
